Derived from Omarchy v3.8.4:

  - the nineteen palettes it ships, in themes/*/colors.toml. The 22 slot keys
    are unchanged from v3.8.4; the names past them (selection, muted, the
    background and foreground shades, orange, brown) are their values from
    Omarchy master, where the palette grew those names. Where the two versions
    overlap they agree, so the two halves are the same colours either way.
  - templates/btop.theme.tpl — unchanged
  - templates/ghostty.conf.tpl — unchanged
  - the {{ key }} / {{ key_strip }} / {{ key_rgb }} template substitutions,
    and rendering them by building a sed script from colors.toml
  - staging generated files in a scratch directory and swapping it into place
    with a single mv

Written for kromi: the app definition format, detection, the link/unlink
commands, and the remaining templates.

A full copy of Omarchy's licence is in LICENSE-omarchy.

The remaining palettes come from elsewhere. What is taken is the colour values
— the 22 slots, transcribed into a colors.toml; the names past them are chosen
here, from that palette's own ramp where it has one. No file, template or code
from any of these projects is carried:

  - themes/dracula      — Dracula, https://github.com/dracula/dracula-theme,
                          Copyright (c) Zeno Rocha, MIT licensed
  - themes/solarized    — Solarized dark, https://github.com/altercation/solarized,
                          Copyright (c) Ethan Schoonover, MIT licensed
  - themes/one-dark     — onedark.vim, https://github.com/joshdick/onedark.vim,
                          Copyright (c) Joshua Dick, MIT licensed
  - themes/aetheria     — Aetheria, https://github.com/JJDizz1L/aetheria,
                          MIT licensed
  - themes/copper-night — Catppuccin Mocha,
                          https://github.com/catppuccin/catppuccin,
                          Copyright (c) Catppuccin, MIT licensed. Every value
                          is a Mocha one: the palette is that ramp on the Crust
                          background with Peach as the accent, which is the
                          arrangement Copper Night chose,
                          https://github.com/hembramnishant50-glitch/omarchy-coppernight-theme
  - themes/retro-pc     — Omarchy RetroPC theme,
